target:    .github/workflows/ci.yml
gate:      php tests/perf-gate-integrity-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    does not NEGATE the contains()
rationale: The half a version list cannot express. Same line, same two versions, opposite lane set: continue-on-error is FALSE where a lane blocks, so dropping the `!` blocks the six interior version-drift lanes and softens the committed baseline and the newest WordPress -- precisely the two the flip exists to make blocking. A check that only compared the list would report this as correct.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@
         # everything, dropping either version, or reverting to a bare `true` all
         # fail that gate. §7 used to match only the literal `continue-on-error:
         # true`, so before this commit it would have matched nothing here.
-        continue-on-error: ${{ !contains(fromJSON('["6.4","7.1"]'), matrix.wp) }}
+        continue-on-error: ${{ contains(fromJSON('["6.4","7.1"]'), matrix.wp) }}
         env:
           # wp-env creates a fresh WordPress with default admin credentials.
           # Override WP_ADMIN_USER / WP_ADMIN_PASS in global-setup.ts.
